{"description":"<p><i>Scaramouche</i> tells the tale of André-Louis Moreau, a young lawyer in Brittany. When his friend is killed by an unremorseful landowner, Moreau swears revenge and begins a life of adventure on the run. His travels lead him to joining a traveling theater troupe, becoming a master swordsman, and even to revolution.</p><p>While the story of <i>Scaramouche</i> is fiction, Sabatini was always very careful to portray history as accurately as he could in his novels. Thus, the backdrop of the French Revolution is vibrant, immediate, and carefully described. In general Sabatini’s prose is sharp and entertaining.</p><p><i>Scaramouche</i> was incredibly popular in its day, and was Sabatini’s most famous novel. The first line is written on Sabatini’s grave.</p>","chapters":[{"title":"I: The Republican","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":3154},{"title":"II: The Aristocrat","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":3502},{"title":"III: The Eloquence of M. de Vilmorin","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":3133},{"title":"IV: The Heritage","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":1786},{"title":"V: The Lord of Gavrillac","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":1490},{"title":"VI: The Windmill","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":2761},{"title":"VII: The Wind","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":4679},{"title":"VIII: Omnes Omnibus","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":2851},{"title":"IX: The Aftermath","part":"Book I: The Robe","words":3343},{"title":"I: The Trespassers","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":5416},{"title":"II: The Service of Thespis","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":2732},{"title":"III: The Comic Muse","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":3823},{"title":"IV: Exit Monsieur Parvissimus","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":2733},{"title":"V: Enter Scaramouche","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":2969},{"title":"VI: Climène","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":4872},{"title":"VII: The Conquest of Nantes","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":3311},{"title":"VIII: The Dream","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":2278},{"title":"IX: The Awakening","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":6392},{"title":"X: Contrition","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":3054},{"title":"XI: The Fracas at the Théâtre Feydau","part":"Book II: The Buskin","words":5557},{"title":"I: Transition","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":5597},{"title":"II: Quos Deus Vult Perdere","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":4575},{"title":"III: President Le Chapelier","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3337},{"title":"IV: Interlude","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":1961},{"title":"V: At Meudon","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":4061},{"title":"VI: Madame de Plougastel","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3346},{"title":"VII: Politicians","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3113},{"title":"VIII: The Spadassinicides","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3641},{"title":"IX: The Paladin of the Third","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2739},{"title":"X: Torn Pride","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":4216},{"title":"XI: The Returning Carriage","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3179},{"title":"XII: Inferences","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2455},{"title":"XIII: Towards the Climax","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2501},{"title":"XIV: The Overwhelming Reason","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":5708},{"title":"XV: Sanctuary","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2843},{"title":"XVI: The Barrier","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":3244},{"title":"XVII: Safe-Conduct","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2528},{"title":"XVIII: Sunrise","part":"Book III: The Sword","words":2150}]}